# Build artefacts
build/
release/
*.o
*.lst
hatari.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The original game and everything derived from it.
#
# This repository deliberately contains NO game data from Ocean / Digital Image
# Design - neither the originals nor extracted, decompressed or rendered
# versions of them. Users bring their own copy; see the README.
assets/
re/resources/
re/unpacked/
re/listings/

# Hatari-Laufzeitartefakte im release-Verzeichnis
*.ini
*-dbg.txt
frame.bin

# DOS oracle (docs/DOS-ORACLE.md): the built disk image embeds the game, and the
# img/ tree holds the genuine MS-DOS 6.22 floppies. Neither belongs in the repo
# under the no-game-data rule above; both are rebuilt by
#   python tools/dos/build_dos_hdd.py
img/
build/img_build/
build/qemu_out/

# Tool scratch
.pi/

# Scratch captures and debug dumps that the emulator and capture helpers
# drop beside the sources. Anchored at the root: committed images live in
# subdirectories, which the leading / does not reach.
/*.png
/*.ppm
/hatari.out.txt
/hatari.err.txt

# Finder metadata, from the macOS side of the toolchain. Unanchored: these
# appear in whatever directory was browsed, not just the root.
.DS_Store
